{
  "assembly_notes": "Four-wheel golf cart. One rigid chassis root carries the body, floor, roof posts, canopy, battery bay and both axles. Each front wheel spins CONTINUOUS on its own steer_knuckle, and each knuckle turns REVOLUTE (+z) on the chassis; the rear wheels spin CONTINUOUS straight off the chassis, so the steered-front / driven-rear layout is fixed. screen_build changes the folding windshield (split_fold, center_fold, full_width) and reports how many leaves it hangs, while canopy_build independently changes what holds the canopy's front edge: vertical posts off the cowl behind the screen, or raked A-posts with a crossbar ahead of it. The A-posts stand outboard of every screen leaf, so both canopies combine with all three screens. seat_build changes the cushions over the battery bay (bench, bucket_pair, rear_facing, rear_deck_row, the last riding on its own raised deck and step board), each hinged on the chassis, and row_count repeats the whole row once more behind it. steer_build is the driver control that turns both knuckles: a dished wheel on a raked column, or an upright tiller on its own steering link. bed_build closes the cargo deck with a hinged tailgate or leaves it an open flatbed with side rails; its length is derived from row_count so a second row always fits. wheelbase_m, track_width_m and wheel_radius_m are the independent parameters; palette, badges and tread grooves are non-core.",
